## C4: arguments the program refuses before any cloud call (exit 2)
$ docker run --rm --network none l14ex/translation-demo:local python -m translation_demo batch --plan --input-uri gs://YOUR_INPUT_BUCKET/run-001/passage.txt --dest xx --output-uri gs://YOUR_OUTPUT_BUCKET/run-001/ 2>&1 | tail -1
__main__.py: error: Choose a supported destination language.
[exit 0]

$ docker run --rm --network none l14ex/translation-demo:local python -m translation_demo batch --plan --input-uri gs://YOUR_INPUT_BUCKET/run-001/passage.txt --dest xx --output-uri gs://YOUR_OUTPUT_BUCKET/run-001/ >/dev/null 2>&1; echo "exit status: $?"
exit status: 2
[exit 0]

$ docker run --rm --network none l14ex/translation-demo:local python -m translation_demo batch --plan --input-uri gs://YOUR_INPUT_BUCKET/run-001/passage.txt --output-uri gs://YOUR_OUTPUT_BUCKET 2>&1 | tail -1
__main__.py: error: A bucket and an object path or output prefix are required.
[exit 0]

$ docker run --rm --network none l14ex/translation-demo:local python -m translation_demo batch --plan --input-uri YOUR_INPUT_BUCKET/run-001/passage.txt --output-uri gs://YOUR_OUTPUT_BUCKET/run-001/ 2>&1 | tail -1
__main__.py: error: Use a gs://bucket/object-or-prefix URI.
